# EOL policy (2026-07 hardening): the index is LF; shell scripts and gradlew MUST stay LF or
# they break with "bad interpreter" on the Linux CI/prod runners the moment a Windows
# contributor without core.autocrlf=input commits them. Windows cmd scripts stay CRLF.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Tessellated-frame text goldens (crates/vike-chart/tests/tessellation_goldens.rs) — compared
# line-by-line by a test. `* text=auto` already normalizes them to LF in the index, but a Windows
# checkout with core.autocrlf=true would materialize CRLF and redden every golden at once, with a
# diff in which no line looks different. Pinned explicitly so the working copy matches the index.
# (The comparator ALSO trims trailing \r — belt and braces, since this rule cannot retroactively
# fix a working copy checked out before it existed.)
crates/vike-chart/tests/goldens/*.txt text eol=lf

# The vendored GUI fonts: TTFs, their licence texts and the icon font's stylesheet, each
# byte-compared against its upstream release by scripts/fonts_vendor_drift.sh and SHA-256-pinned by
# crates/vike-ui-theme/src/fonts.rs. Never converted: a CRLF checkout of a licence text or of the
# stylesheet would read as drift, and fail the pin.
assets/fonts/* -text

# The brand files (assets/brand/SOURCES.md): generated from vike_ui_theme::brand and compared by
# crates/vike-ui-theme/tests/brand_assets.rs — the SVGs and the desktop entry byte for byte, so a
# CRLF checkout would read as drift. Never converted.
assets/brand/** -text

# The two SURFACE fixtures — the command surface and the run profile's schema, both rendered from
# Rust tables and both VENDORED byte-identically by the documentation site. `* text=auto` already
# normalizes them to LF in the index, and each one's own gate compares PARSED JSON rather than
# bytes, so a CRLF working copy would not redden a test — it would silently make the vendored copy
# differ from the published asset. Pinned for the same reason as the goldens above: the working
# copy must match the index.
crates/vike-cli/tests/fixtures/cli.json text eol=lf
crates/vike-backtest/tests/fixtures/profile.json text eol=lf

# The strategy the two live builder smokes SEND. Its sha256 is the artifact's content address on
# the deployed box, so a CRLF working copy would be a DIFFERENT sha with no visible difference — a
# cold compile and a new file on production instead of the cache hit both smokes are shaped for
# (`crates/vike-strategy-builder/tests/builder_live_smoke.rs`'s `strategy_source` says why).
crates/vike-strategy-builder/tests/fixtures/*.rs.in text eol=lf

# Binaries — never EOL-normalized (git auto-detects, this makes it explicit for the committed
# jar the CI drift gate byte-compares).
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
# The datahub wire's frozen protocol frames (crates/vike-datahub-client/tests/wire_tag_fixtures.rs)
# — a big-endian u32 length prefix in front of each JSON body. Git's own heuristic already calls
# them binary (the prefixes carry NUL bytes), but these bytes ARE the contract: an EOL rewrite would
# change a body's length without changing its prefix and desync the stream, so it is stated rather
# than left to detection.
fixtures/datahub_wire/*.frames binary
